      "checks": [
        "Ledger HistoricalDocument112-141 keeps a final lease and Pin separate from optional payload. verifyCurrent119-124 performs the existing lease identity check. read126-129 qualifies that custody before a cold exact full bounded read/hash/path; releasePayload137-139 also calls existing releaseOriginalBytes and drops only snapshot residency, not HANDLE custody.",
        "leaseHistorical144-164 validates actual bytes/SHA/path, rebinds the expected ExactRef object in Pin and closes on failure. Store542-556 distinguishes payload reads from proof-only metadata/Pin/root qualification. No new authority or permission is created by the historical-only type.",
        "Ordinary LeasedDocument/Document bodies and identity/alias/defensive-copy contracts remain distinct from detached historical cold snapshots. Exactly-once closure in the answer is resource-lifetime shorthand, not a proof that every Java close method can only be invoked once; underlying close guards and Store closePair/finish preserve cleanup behavior.",
        "The answer compresses firstFailure handling: existing carried cause/identity paths avoid duplicate/self suppression, while cleanup errors remain aggregated. finish is not a payload rehash. The finite summary does not replace all failure-path source or software evidence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "B",
      "classification": "EMPTY_FINDINGS_BOUNDED_ACCOUNTING_AND_TRACE_SUMMARY_WITH_TERMINOLOGY_LIMIT",
      "new_reachable_findings": 0,
      "checks": [
        "Store404-418 rotates only payloads FIFO, subtracting exact released residency and removing that FIFO cell; proof entries and pair custody stay insertion ordered. Entry/handle counts420-421 include unchanged external-source custody. Cold refill is admitted only if makePayloadRoom permits it and records its snapshot once.",
        "Store558-586 first requires room for mandatory metadata, combines its payload with Math.addExact and can retire the new payload while retaining its actual pair proof. If metadata cannot fit, it closes the unretained pair. The summary does not mean every arithmetic update uses Math.addExact: some updates use bounded room inequalities under finite limits.",
        "Store807-825 keeps fresh qualification on held reads, retains optional payload separately, and keeps original entry/handle minus4 headroom. verifyRetainedDependencies430-449 invokes proof-only verifyLeasedPublication551-556, never HistoricalDocument.read. Zero payload reload on that path is a source-callgraph statement, not a disk IO counter result.",
        "allRetained=false is absorbing for a dependency trace; capacity fallback is not itself an exception or firstFailure poison of the whole scope. The answer calls it a poisoned trace imprecisely. Missing custody, scope failure, and an older independently verified prefix are separate states.",
